The implementation of governmental affairs in the field of Women Empowerment and Child Protection aims to increase efforts to Protect women's rights, fulfill children's rights and Special Protection for Children and to increase the role of Regional Government and the business world, media and the community in efforts to Empower Women and Protect Children. The main material contained in the body of the Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Women and Children Empowerment and Protection includes:

a. fulfillment of women's rights;
b. women empowerment;
c. women protection; d. child protection;
e. fulfillment of children's rights;
f. integrated service center; g. safe house;
h. child-friendly regency;
i. guidance and supervision; j. community participation;
k. awards; and
l. financing.
