To ensure the fulfillment of the rights of women and children, regional governments are obligated and responsible to implement and support national policies in the administration of governmental affairs in the field of women and children empowerment and protection in the region. In addition, regional governments are also given the obligation to supervise the implementation of women and children empowerment and protection.

The implementation of women and children empowerment and protection is an effort to realize capable women and an effort to protect women and children from all acts of violence in order to achieve the goal of welfare. Women and children empowerment and protection that has been implemented so far has not been optimal and comprehensive in reaching the problems faced by women and children. In addition, public awareness of efforts to empower and protect women and children is still very lacking. To achieve these objectives and to implement the authority of regional governments as outlined in Law

